    {%- when 'overview' -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        Task 27.1 — the Portal_Home.

        ── THE GREETING IS SERVER-RENDERED, AND IS THE LCP ──────────────────────
        It comes from Liquid's `customer.first_name` with NO script dependency
        (Requirement 4.1), so the largest contentful paint happens in the HTML
        response and does not wait on a bundle, a token or an App Proxy round trip.
        It is a `<p>` and not a heading because the chrome already owns the page's
        one `<h1>`; a second would break the outline for the sake of a font size.

        ── OMIT, DO NOT EMPTY — AND DO NOT REVEAL ───────────────────────────────
        §21.6 sets two absolute rules that look contradictory until you read the
        third: content is never inserted above existing content, no element appears
        on hydration that the server render lacked, and a tile that turns out to be
        empty is REMOVED rather than revealed. So every tile below is server-rendered
        with a skeleton at its exact final geometry, and the module either fills that
        same box or deletes it. Nothing is ever added.

        ── NOT A GRID OF CARDS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
        §18.5 names the anti-card rule and lists the only three permitted cards. A
        balance is a numeral and a badge on the page; an order is a ruled row; a
        wishlist item is an image and text in a grid cell. Exactly one thing here is
        a card, and that is the reward — a discrete offer with a price and an action.

        ── NO CUSTOMER IDENTIFIER IS EMITTED ────────────────────────────────────
        No `customerId` in a config block, a data attribute or a query string. The
        App Proxy signs the customer into every request; an id in the DOM would be a
        second, forgeable channel for the one fact that must not be client-supplied.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <p class="athoor-overview__greeting" data-portal-greeting>
        {%- if customer.first_name != blank -%}
          Welcome back, {{ customer.first_name }}
        {%- else -%}
          Welcome back
        {%- endif -%}
      </p>

      {%- comment -%}
        Balance, tier and progress (Requirements 4.2, 4.3). The numeral line and its
        label reserve their own height, and the 6 px progress track is rendered
        server-side so the fill can be set once without transitioning a width.
