      </section>

      <template data-portal-row="overview-recent">
        <li class="athoor-overview__recent-item">
          <a data-slot="link" href="#">
            <span class="athoor-portal__image-box">
              <img class="athoor-portal__image" data-slot="image" alt="" width="300" height="300" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
            </span>
            <span class="athoor-portal__row-meta" data-slot="title"></span>
          </a>
        </li>
      </template>
    {%- when 'settings' -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        Task 26.1.

        WHAT THIS ARM DOES *NOT* CONTAIN, AND WHY. Task 26.1 describes
        "communication, notification and privacy preferences as toggles". Only
        communication exists on the wire: `PortalCommunicationPreferences` is four
        booleans, `push_enabled` is a reserved column that appears in no contract and
        is explicitly refused a wire name, and privacy in this design is not a toggle
        at all — it is the two ACTIONS below (request a copy, request deletion).
        Inventing a notification toggle would mean inventing a field name the design
        declines to specify, so there is one toggle group here, not three.

        NO CREDENTIAL CONTROL (Requirement 13.7). No password entry, change or reset,
        and no email input — the store uses Shopify's new customer accounts, which
        authenticate by emailed code, so both route to Shopify's own experience.

        Every preference states its PURPOSE at the point of collection
        (Requirement 23.8): the purpose is beside the toggle, not in a policy page
        the customer has to go and find.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <section class="athoor-settings__group" data-portal-comms aria-labelledby="AthoorSettingsCommsTitle" hidden>
        <h2 class="athoor-fragrance__heading" id="AthoorSettingsCommsTitle">What we send you</h2>
        <ul class="athoor-settings__list" role="list" data-portal-comms-list></ul>
      </section>

      <template data-portal-row="setting">
        <li class="athoor-settings__item">
          <label class="athoor-settings__switch">
            <input type="checkbox" data-portal-comms-toggle>
            <span class="athoor-settings__switch-text">
              <span class="athoor-settings__switch-label" data-slot="label"></span>
              {%- comment -%}
                The purpose, at the point of collection (Requirement 23.8). Linked by
                `aria-describedby` so it is read with the control rather than after it.
              {%- endcomment -%}
              <span class="athoor-portal__row-meta" data-slot="purpose"></span>
            </span>
          </label>
        </li>
      </template>

      {%- comment -%}
        Marketing consent is SEPARATE from the toggles above, and deliberately so:
        it is Shopify's to store, it is written through its own endpoint, and its
        state carries a date the others do not have (Requirement 13.3). Presenting it
        inside the same list would imply one store behind all five controls.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <section class="athoor-settings__group" data-portal-consent aria-labelledby="AthoorSettingsConsentTitle" hidden>
        <h2 class="athoor-fragrance__heading" id="AthoorSettingsConsentTitle">Marketing email</h2>
        <p class="athoor-portal__row-meta" id="AthoorSettingsConsentPurpose">
          Offers, new arrivals and private-client invitations. You can withdraw at any time.
        </p>
        <label class="athoor-settings__switch">
          <input type="checkbox" data-portal-consent-toggle aria-describedby="AthoorSettingsConsentPurpose AthoorSettingsConsentState">
          <span class="athoor-settings__switch-label">Send me marketing email</span>
        </label>
        <p class="athoor-portal__row-status" id="AthoorSettingsConsentState" data-portal-consent-state></p>
      </section>

      {%- comment -%}
        Requirement 13.5 as task 26.1 scopes it: the address COUNT and a route to the
        editor. The editor itself lives in Profile — a second copy here would be two
        implementations of one form, and the one that drifts is the one nobody tests.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <section class="athoor-settings__group" data-portal-addresses aria-labelledby="AthoorSettingsAddressesTitle">
        <h2 class="athoor-fragrance__heading" id="AthoorSettingsAddressesTitle">Delivery addresses</h2>
        <p class="athoor-portal__row-meta" data-portal-address-count></p>
        <a class="athoor-portal__action" href="/pages/my-athoor-profile" data-portal-address-route>
          Manage your addresses
        </a>
      </section>

      {%- comment -%}
        Requirement 13.8 — a route to request a copy of the data, and a route to
        request deletion. Both are rate limited server-side, so both render a designed
        wait state rather than failing silently or inviting a second press.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <section class="athoor-settings__group" data-portal-privacy aria-labelledby="AthoorSettingsPrivacyTitle">
        <h2 class="athoor-fragrance__heading" id="AthoorSettingsPrivacyTitle">Your data</h2>

        <div class="athoor-settings__action">
          <p class="athoor-portal__row-meta" id="AthoorSettingsExportPurpose">
            A machine-readable copy of everything this account holds about you.
          </p>
          <button
            class="athoor-portal__action"
            type="button"
            data-portal-export
            aria-describedby="AthoorSettingsExportPurpose AthoorSettingsExportResult"
          >Request a copy of your data</button>
          <p class="athoor-portal__row-meta" id="AthoorSettingsExportResult" data-portal-export-result aria-live="polite" hidden></p>
        </div>

        <div class="athoor-settings__action">
          <p class="athoor-portal__row-meta" id="AthoorSettingsErasurePurpose">
            Ask us to delete your account data. A member of our team will action this and contact you.
          </p>
          <button
            class="athoor-portal__action athoor-settings__action--grave"
            type="button"
            data-portal-erasure-open
            aria-describedby="AthoorSettingsErasurePurpose"
          >Request deletion of your data</button>
          <p class="athoor-portal__row-status" data-portal-erasure-result aria-live="polite" hidden></p>
        </div>
      </section>

      {%- comment -%}
        Deletion is confirmed in the ONE sheet implementation of task 18.5. It is not
        reversible from the customer's side once the request is recorded, so it does
        not happen on a single press.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <dialog class="athoor-portal__sheet" data-portal-erasure-sheet aria-labelledby="AthoorErasureSheetTitle">
        <div class="athoor-portal__sheet-inner">
          <h2 class="athoor-portal__sheet-title" id="AthoorErasureSheetTitle" data-portal-sheet-heading>Request deletion</h2>
          <p>We will remove your account data and contact you when it is done. Your order records are kept where the law requires it.</p>
          <p class="athoor-portal__row-meta">This cannot be undone from here.</p>
          <button class="athoor-portal__action athoor-settings__action--grave" type="button" data-portal-erasure-confirm>
            Yes, request deletion
          </button>
          <button class="athoor-portal__sheet-dismiss" type="button" data-portal-sheet-dismiss>Cancel</button>
        </div>
      </dialog>

      {%- comment -%}
        Requirement 13.6 — the logout control, ending the Shopify session and
        returning to the storefront. `routes.account_logout_url` is Shopify's own
        indirection: hardcoding `/account/logout` would be wrong under new customer
        accounts, which is exactly the mode this store runs.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <section class="athoor-settings__group athoor-settings__group--last" aria-labelledby="AthoorSettingsSessionTitle">
        <h2 class="athoor-fragrance__heading" id="AthoorSettingsSessionTitle">This device</h2>
        <a class="athoor-portal__action" href="{{ routes.account_logout_url }}" data-portal-logout rel="nofollow">
          Sign out
        </a>
      </section>
  {%- endcase -%}
</section>
